{"type":"system","subtype":"hook_response","hook_id":"7bcf4a84-2270-4ef1-9292-ec5e21681932","hook_name":"SessionStart:startup","hook_event":"SessionStart","output":"<!-- CLAUDE.md (filtered for: critical-context, execution-rules, what-map, summary, file-naming, environment, memory-context-tools, memory-search, platform) -->\n\n<platform>\n## Platform: Windows\r\n\r\nThis is a Windows environment. Always use PowerShell-compatible syntax for shell commands. Avoid Unix-specific line continuations (`\\`), path separators (`/` in shell commands), and bash-specific features (extglob, etc.). When writing scripts, prefer `.ps1` or `.cmd` files over `.sh` files. Test commands mentally for Windows compatibility before executing.\n</platform>\n\n<critical-context>\n## CRITICAL �?\" Must Follow Always\r\n- **CRITICAL:** Use `uv` for all Python operations. Never use `pip` directly or base environment.\r\n- **CRITICAL:** Read a file before editing it. Never edit without reading first.\r\n- **CRITICAL:** Archive instead of delete. Never permanently delete without explicit user approval.\r\n- **CRITICAL:** Search claude-mem FIRST before answering personal/business questions. Fall back to MemPalace/QMD if no results.\n</critical-context>\n\n<execution-rules>\n## Execution Rules\r\n\r\n- When a plan has been created and approved, EXECUTE it immediately. Do not ask which step to start with.\r\n- When the user asks to install or set up something, actually complete the installation �?\" do not claim completion without verification.\r\n- Prefer the user's explicitly requested approach first. Only pivot to alternatives after the requested approach demonstrably fails.\n</execution-rules>\n\n<what-map>\n## WHAT �?\" Map\r\n\r\n- **Workspace:** `C:\\Users\\Jyue` �?\" home workspace (thinking layer)\r\n- **Identity:** `.claude/agents/identity/`\r\n- **Skills:** `.claude/skills/` (canonical); junction at `.cursor/skills/`\r\n- **Execution:** Notion �?\" tasks/tracking live there\r\n- **Platfor